From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cube oakley <cube-oakley@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:09:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] software_isp: Gather GPU statistics over the visible
 input

The GPU debayer scales the whole input to the output size, cropping only
what the aspect ratio does not fit, but it set the statistics window to
an output-sized rectangle at the origin, which suits only the CPU
debayer's crop. At 1280x960 or 1920x1080 from a 4000x3000 frame, AGC,
AWB and autofocus saw only the top-left corner: the autofocus sharpness
curve was flat (about 5% across the lens range) while the same scene at
full resolution peaked fivefold. Use the visible part of the input.

[Derek Ross: the projection anchors the scaled input at the origin, so
 the visible part starts at the origin rather than being centred.]

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_egl.cpp | 17 ++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_egl.cpp b/src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_egl.cpp
index 1f26901..5a8a490 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_egl.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_egl.cpp
@@ -340,10 +340,21 @@ int DebayerEGL::configure(const StreamConfiguration &inputCfg,
 	window_.height = outputCfg.size.height;
 
 	/*
-	 * Don't pass x,y from window_ since process() already adjusts for it.
-	 * But crop the window to 2/3 of its width and height for speedup.
+	 * The shader scales the whole input to the output size and crops only
+	 * what the aspect ratio does not fit, so gather statistics over that
+	 * visible part of the input. An output-sized window, as the CPU
+	 * debayer's crop uses, would cover only the top-left corner of a
+	 * downscaled frame and starve AGC, AWB and autofocus. The projection in
+	 * setShaderVariableValues() anchors the scaled input at the origin, so
+	 * the crop falls on the right and bottom of the input.
 	 */
-	stats_->setWindow(Rectangle(window_.size()));
+	const float scale = std::max(static_cast<float>(outputCfg.size.width) / nativeOutputSize_.width,
+				     static_cast<float>(outputCfg.size.height) / nativeOutputSize_.height);
+	const Size visible(std::min(inputCfg.size.width,
+				    static_cast<unsigned int>(outputCfg.size.width / scale)),
+			   std::min(inputCfg.size.height,
+				    static_cast<unsigned int>(outputCfg.size.height / scale)));
+	stats_->setWindow(Rectangle(visible));
 
 	inputBufferCount_ = inputCfg.bufferCount;
 	outputBufferCount_ = outputCfg.bufferCount;
